parts.memo:
1 mark for point raised that with some thought on the side of the examiner might be valid. Examples:
- Bribes/irrecoverable loans imply that banks must charge higher rates on other productive loans to make up for the losses suffered;
- Economic uncertainty implies higher future losses through potential bad debts that must be recouped through higher interest rates;
- Land is often the security for bank loans. If ownership is uncertain then security is uncertain and higher interest rates called for;
- Modern monetary theory, as called for by many radical economists, imply the potential for higher inflation that is a critical component of interest rates;

2 marks if a valid point is raised and well explained. No thinking/guessing is required on the part of the examiner.
